# Codex OPUS-CODEX-20261015-11 Q2 and the author (LMX_blog/2026-10-15.md): `c: tick()` is an ordinary named Structure
# retaining tick's application. `c()`, `c: ()` and the vertical `c:` closed by `---` are one Frame with an empty
# argument Structure: on the named Structure c each is its empty write after admission, never its execution -- tick
# does not run (84 if it did): exit 7.
int: ticks 0
fn: tick () int
    node\ticks: node\ticks + 1
    return: 2
end: tick
fn: check () int
    c: tick()
    c()
    c: ()
    c:
    ---
    if: node\ticks != 0
        return: 84
    return: 7
end: check
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: check(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
